 "Ponytail holders are doing overtime.": "Poniestert-rekkies doen oortyd.",
 "Postcard weather. You're welcome.": "Poskaart weer. Plesier.",
 "Prettiest blue sky in the country, and it feels like a fridge with a view.": "Mooiste blou lug in die land, en dit voel soos 'n yskas met uitsig.",
 "Pretty evening, if you like walls.": "Mooi aand, as jy van mure hou.",
 "Pretty evening. Deeply uninhabitable.": "Mooi aand. Diep onbewoonbaar.",
 "Proper storm. Not the pretty kind.": "Ordentlike storm. Nie die mooi soort nie.",
 "Quiet out there. Almost suspicious.": "Stil daarbuite. Byna verdag.",
 "Rain came all the way home.": "Die reën het die hele pad saam huis toe gekom.",
 "Rain coming off the roof in one solid sheet: the stoep has a curtain tonight.": "Reën wat in een soliede laken van die dak afkom: die stoep het vanaand 'n gordyn.",
 "Rain on a farm isn't weather. It's a salary falling from the sky.": "Reën op 'n plaas is nie weer nie. Dis 'n salaris wat val.",
 "Rain on an otherwise good-looking evening.": "Reën op 'n andersins mooi aand.",
 "Rain out here is an event; the whole veld will smell of it by seven.": "Reën hier buite is 'n gebeurtenis; die hele veld gaan teen sewe daarna ruik.",
 "Rain so heavy it should pay rent.": "Reën so swaar dit moet huur betaal.",
 "Rain this hard, even the taxis start indicating.": "Reën só hard, selfs die taxi's sit hul flikkers aan.",
 "Rain through a streetlight looks like static, and tonight the whole street is tuned to it.": "Reën deur 'n straatlig lyk soos ruis, en vanaand is die hele straat daarop ingestel.",
 "Rain turns every South African driver back into a learner. Hazards on, dignity off.": "Reën verander elke Suid-Afrikaanse bestuurder terug in 'n leerling.",
 "Rain was the warning. This is the follow-through.": "Die reën was die waarskuwing. Dit is die opvolg.",
 "Rain? Possibly. Commitment? Never.": "Reën? Moontlik. Sal ek my lewe daar op wed? Nooit.",
 "Red sky at night, shepherd's delight — tomorrow just got a good reference.": "Rooi lug saans, mooi weer môre — môre het pas 'n goeie verwysing gekry.",
 "Respect the thunder. It's earned it.": "Respekteer die donder. Hy het dit verdien.",
 "Running weather, honestly: cool, grey, and the sea doing the soundtrack.": "Drafweer, eerlikwaar: koel, grys, en die see doen die klankbaan.",
 "Rusks first. Panic later.": "Beskuit eerste. Paniek later.",
 "Sand in places sand should never be.": "Sand in plekke waar sand nooit moet wees nie.",
 "Saturday energy: maximum. Responsibilities: minimum.": "Saterdagenergie: maksimum. Verantwoordelikhede: minimum.",
 "Saturday evening, and the walk from the front door defeated the whole look.": "Saterdagaand, en die stap van die voordeur af het die hele look verwoes.",
 "Saturday morning, and the sea has already been over that railing twice.": "Saterdagoggend, en die see was al twee keer oor daardie reling.",
 "Saturday night at the sea, and the sea has taken the whole promenade.": "Saterdagaand by die see, en die see het die hele promenade gevat.",
 "Saturday night, and the entertainment is free and about four billion years old.": "Saterdagaand, en die vermaak is verniet en omtrent vier miljard jaar oud.",
 "Saturday, and he is in before seven because by ten it is unusable.": "Saterdag, en hy is voor sewe in, want teen tien is dit onbruikbaar.",
 "Saturday, and neither of them will admit the wind is winning.": "Saterdag, en nie een van hulle wil erken die wind wen nie.",
 "Saturday, and the only shade for the next hour is inside this car.": "Saterdag, en die enigste skaduwee vir die volgende uur is binne hierdie kar.",
 "Saturday, and the only thing on that line doing any work is the pegs.": "Saterdag, en die enigste ding op daardie draad wat werk doen is die pennetjies.",
 "Saturday, and the sky went from orange to blue without one cloud interrupting.": "Saterdag, en die lug het van oranje na blou gegaan sonder dat een wolk hom gesteur het.",
 "Saturday, and the water is still warmer than the air above it.": "Saterdag, en die water is steeds warmer as die lug daarbo.",
 "Saturday, and the wind has strong opinions about your plans for the garden.": "Saterdag, en die wind het sterk menings oor jou planne vir die tuin.",
 "Schrodinger's rain. It both is and isn't.": "Schrödinger se reën. Dit is én is nie.",
 "Serious weather. The rest is postponed.": "Ernstige weer. Die res is uitgestel.",
 "She has found the one tile in this house that has not warmed up yet.": "Sy het die een teël in hierdie huis gekry wat nog nie warm geword het nie.",
 "She is leaning at an angle that a flat path does not normally require.": "Sy leun skuinser as wat 'n plat paadjie ooit behoort te vra.",
 "She is lying on tile rather than anything soft, and that was a decision.": "Sy lê op teël eerder as op iets sags, en dit was 'n besluit.",
 "She is not looking at the washing, she is looking at where it might land.": "Sy kyk nie na die wasgoed nie, sy kyk waar dit dalk gaan land.",
 "She is not looking for anything and both of us know it.": "Sy soek niks nie en ons weet dit albei.",
